          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>World War I and Marconi's Technology</strong><br>\nDuring World War I, Marconi's wireless technology became essential for military communication. His company's equipment was extensively used for coordinating movements and gathering intelligence, which highlighted the strategic importance of wireless communication technology in modern warfare.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Inventions and Innovations</strong><br>\nMarconi continued to innovate throughout his life, working on shortwave wireless communication, which led to the development of microwave transmission. He believed in the possibility of long-distance wireless telephony and even considered the concept of radar before its eventual realization by others.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Marconi's Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nGuglielmo Marconi passed away on July 20, 1937, leaving behind a legacy as the pioneer of wireless communication. His inventions laid the groundwork for modern radio and telecommunications, and his company continued to be a significant force in the field of electronics and communication. Marconi's work revolutionized the way the world exchanges information, making him one of the most influential figures in the history of technology.</p>\n"
              },
